{
  "abstract": "We study one explicit quartic-CM case of the Hodge conjecture for abelian varieties that lies beyond imaginary-quadratic Weil-class methods. Let $\\alpha=(7,10,13,19,22,28)$ be a degree-$33$ Fermat fourfold character and $B_8$ the associated eight-dimensional ramified Prym factor of a cyclic-cover Jacobian. Unconditionally, using exact Frobenius certificates, we show $\\operatorname{End}^0_{\\overline{\\mathbf Q}}(B_8)=E=\\mathbf Q(\\zeta_{33})^{\\langle 4\\rangle}$ and $Hg(B_8)=\\operatorname{Res}_{E^+/\\mathbf Q}SU_E$ with $E^+=\\mathbf Q(\\sqrt{33})$. A structural theorem for balanced special-unitary abelian varieties then gives $\\operatorname{Hdg}^2(B_8)_{\\mathbf Q}=D^2(B_8)\\oplus W_E(B_8)$, where $W_E(B_8)=\\bigwedge_E^4H^1(B_8,\\mathbf Q)$, and shows that the classical and generalized Hodge conjectures for every self-power $B_8^n$ are equivalent to algebraicity of $W_E(B_8)$. The source Fermat block is algebraic, both by a cubic-to-Fermat graph correspondence with cubic-scroll classes and independently by Aoki's level-$66$ identity. Our main contribution is an explicit transfer: a common finite quotient of a Kummer curve product and the Fermat character quotient, a Poincaré curve-to-Prym divisor correspondence, and contraction along the small diagonal of $B_8$ give a single Chow correspondence carrying the source block onto $W_E(B_8)$, with exact normalization $5^{-3}$ relative to canonical Galois descent. This avoids the semiregularity step in secant-sheaf approaches. The transfer is stated conditionally on four fixed-model quotient inputs (H1–H4) whose proofs are written out but have not yet had independent expert review; under them, $W_E(B_8)$ is algebraic and the classical and generalized Hodge conjectures hold for all $B_8^n$. Exact certificates for all discrete computations are supplied. We do not claim the Hodge conjecture for $X_{33}^4$ or in general.",
